  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nAs high pressure continues to drift eastward thru today, \nsouthwest winds will gradually increase. This will be most \npronounced by afternoon, where winds will be breezy and temps \nwill climb well into the 60s and maybe even hit 70 in a few \nspots. The cold front will not cross the area until Fri, so\ntonight will be quite mild for this time of year and especially\nmild compared to recent overnight temperatures. Some locations \nare unlikely to drop out of the 50s, which will be within a few \ndegrees of the record warm min temps for this time of year.\n\nThe frontal passage itself looks to be mostly dry again, but a\na few showers remain possible, especially inland. \n\nAfter the front we return to dry and seasonable weather. Temps \nare expected to be near normal on Halloween, with most areas \nstarting the early evening in the 40s and 50s, falling into the\n30s overnight. Ensembles continue to show a flip to a wetter \nweather pattern to start November, but they also continue to \npush this back in time so there is plenty of time for that to \nchange.",
